! baupla fuzykamni

~tc~ Previous content of "BPFK" page now directed here; please integrate:
An abbreviation for ((baupla fuzykamni)) (Language Planning Commission), a committee of the ((LLG)) whose mission is to publish the ((mini-dictionary)), and various other issues pertaining to the completion of the Lojban language prescription.
~/tc~

The baupla fuzykamni (Language Planning Commission), also known as the ((BPFK)) or ((byfy)), is the definitional committee for the Lojban language, charged with expanding the current documentation of the provisional Lojban baseline (and in particular improving the quality of cmavo definitions) as well as resolving any errors or conflicts that might exist.  It was formed as a result of [http://lojban.org/llg/baseline.html|the new baseline statement] by the ((LLG)) board in November of 2002.  The baupla fuzykamni is currently led (in an administrative capacity, at least) by ((Robin Lee Powell)).

